{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"sunlit-cynical-ray","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Problem\nThe close path (`rebar transition <id> in_progress closed`) acquires the ONE tickets write lock (.ticket-write.lock + .ticket-write.lock.d) and holds it across the LLM completion verifier — a multi-minute agentic operation (observed 15+ min).\n\n## Evidence (2026-08-12, this host)\n- pid 61327 `rebar transition repressive-delectable-swan in_progress closed` held /Users/joeoakhart/rebar/.tickets-tracker/.ticket-write.lock.d from 20:35:52 for 15+ minutes (holder alive and healthy the whole time; stamp: rebar-lock v2 host=name-Joes-MacBook-Pro.local pid=61327).\n- A concurrent session reported it could not close a ticket due to 'long-lasting locks on the tickets branch' during exactly this window.\n- Earlier this session: an implementer lost 3 plan-review runs to flock contention from sibling agents; the lock-retry work (REBAR_LOCK_RETRIES, change cc69cc1179) treats the symptom (acquire timeouts) not the cause (verifier-length holds).\n\n## Root-cause direction (operator-specified)\nThe close operation should NOT hold the write lock during the LLM completion verifier. Restructure to: run the verification BEFORE acquiring the write lock, then acquire, re-check the cheap invariants (status unchanged, attestation/current-material still valid — optimistic concurrency already exists on status), append the transition event, release. The lock should bracket only the store mutation, not the LLM phase.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] The write lock is not held during any LLM call on the close path (verify with a test that asserts lock-dir absence while the verifier stub runs, or equivalent instrumentation).\n- [ ] Optimistic re-check under the lock prevents TOCTOU: a status/material change between verify and append fails the close with exit 10 (ConcurrencyError semantics), not a silent stale write.\n- [ ] Existing close-gate semantics unchanged: signature recording, --ref retargeting, force_close_reason, and the completion precheck behave identically.\n- [ ] Concurrent-close regression test: two closes on different tickets do not serialize on the LLM phase.\n","id":"84af-8d4f-bc1c-41b9","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"transition close holds the tickets write lock for the whole LLM completion verification"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786592907556540001,"uuid":"93bdd0b2-a009-4844-8eed-958ea3092239"}